\boxed{\text{In an unrestricted MP2 (UMP2) calculation the reference wavefunction is an unrestricted Hartree–Fock (UHF) determinant. For open‑shell species the UHF wavefunction allows the α and β electrons to occupy different spatial orbitals, which lowers the energy but destroys spin purity: the determinant is not an eigenfunction of the total spin operator } \hat S^{2}. \text{Consequently the UHF reference is contaminated by higher‑spin components (e.g., a doublet mixed with quartet character). The MP2 correlation correction is built on this spin‑contaminated reference and does not restore proper spin symmetry, so the resulting UMP2 energies inherit the contamination. This problem is especially acute for radicals (CH₃·) and transition‑state structures (TS₁, TS₂, TS₃) that often exhibit near‑degenerate frontier orbitals or diradical character, which amplify spin mixing. Hence UMP2 energies for these open‑shell species can be unreliable unless spin‑contamination is checked (e.g., via ⟨S²⟩) or a spin‑adapted method such as RO‑MP2 is used.}}
\]

