&\mathbf r=
\begin{pmatrix}\mathbf r_{1}\\ \mathbf r_{2}\end{pmatrix}
=
\mathbf T\,\boldsymbol{\xi},
\qquad 
\mathbf T=
\begin{pmatrix}
\mathbf I&-\tfrac12\mathbf I\\[2pt]
\mathbf I&\tfrac12\mathbf I
\end{pmatrix},
\qquad 
\mathbf S\equiv\mathbf T^{-1}=
\begin{pmatrix}
\frac12\mathbf I&\frac12\mathbf I\\[2pt]
-\mathbf I&\mathbf I
\end{pmatrix}.
\\[6pt]
&\text{Mobility in }(\mathbf R,\mathbf Q)\text{ space:}\\
&\widetilde{\mathbf M}(\boldsymbol\xi)=\mathbf S\,\mathbf M(\mathbf r_{1},\mathbf r_{2})\,\mathbf S^{\!T},
\qquad 
