\[
\boxed{
\begin{aligned}
\frac{\partial\psi(\mathbf Q,\mathbf R,t)}{\partial t}
=&-\nabla_{\mathbf R}\!\cdot\!\bigl[V_{R}\,\psi\bigr]
-\nabla_{\mathbf Q}\!\cdot\!\bigl[V_{Q}\,\psi\bigr] \\[4pt]
&+\nabla_{\mathbf R}\!\cdot\!\Bigl[
\mathbf D_{RR}\!\cdot\!\nabla_{\mathbf R}\psi
+\mathbf D_{RQ}\!\cdot\!\nabla_{\mathbf Q}\psi\Bigr] \\[4pt]
&+\nabla_{\mathbf Q}\!\cdot\!\Bigl[
\mathbf D_{QR}\!\cdot\!\nabla_{\mathbf R}\psi
+\mathbf D_{QQ}\!\cdot\!\nabla_{\mathbf Q}\psi\Bigr].
\end{aligned}
}
\]

Equivalently, in compact tensor notation,

\[
\boxed{
\frac{\partial\psi}{\partial t}
=-\nabla_{\boldsymbol\xi}\!\cdot\!\Bigl[\,
\bigl(\mathbf V^{\rm flow}(\boldsymbol\xi)-\widetilde{\mathbf M}(\boldsymbol\xi)\nabla_{\boldsymbol\xi}U(\boldsymbol\xi)\bigr)\psi
-\nabla_{\boldsymbol\xi}\!\cdot\!\bigl(\mathbf D(\boldsymbol\xi)\psi\bigr)\Bigr].
}
\]

Here \(\mathbf M_{ij}\) contains the Rotne–Prager–Yamakawa tensor for bead–bead hydrodynamic interactions and the Blake image tensor for bead–wall interactions; \(U\) is the sum of the FENE spring potential and the two wall potentials. The equation therefore incorporates (i) convection by the imposed shear flow and by the HI‑induced drift of each bead, (ii) the conservative forces from the FENE spring and the wall, and (iii) the configuration‑dependent diffusion tensor arising from the full hydrodynamic interaction.

