The contribution of the two disordered Cl sites (occupancies 0.6 and 0.4) to the structure factor for a reflection \((hkl)\) is the occupancy‑weighted sum of their individual atomic contributions.  If the primary Cl position is \(\mathbf{r}_{\rm Cl}=(x_{\rm Cl},y_{\rm Cl},z_{\rm Cl})\) and the second site is related by the translation \(\mathbf t=(\tfrac12,0,\tfrac12)\), then  

\[
\begin{aligned}
F_{\rm Cl}(hkl)&=f_{\rm Cl}\Big[0.6\,e^{2\pi i\,(h x_{\rm Cl}+k y_{\rm Cl}+l z_{\rm Cl})}
+0.4\,e^{2\pi i\,[h(x_{\rm Cl}+½)+k y_{\rm Cl}+l(z_{\rm Cl}+½)]}\Big] \\
&=f_{\rm Cl}\,e^{2\pi i\,(h x_{\rm Cl}+k y_{\rm Cl}+l z_{\rm Cl})}
\Big[0.6+0.4\,e^{2\pi i\,(h\cdot½+l\cdot½)}\Big] \\
&=f_{\rm Cl}\,e^{2\pi i\,(h x_{\rm Cl}+k y_{\rm Cl}+l z_{\rm Cl})}
\Big[0.6+0.4\,e^{\pi i\,(h+l)}\Big] \\
&=f_{\rm Cl}\,e^{2\pi i\,(h x_{\rm Cl}+k y_{\rm Cl}+l z_{\rm Cl})}
\Big[0.6+0.4\,(-1)^{\,h+l}\Big].
\end{aligned}
\]

\[
\boxed{F_{\mathrm{Cl}}(hkl)=f_{\mathrm{Cl}}\;e^{2\pi i\,(h x_{\mathrm{Cl}}+k y_{\mathrm{Cl}}+l z_{\mathrm{Cl}})}\big[\,0.6+0.4\,(-1)^{\,h+l}\big]}
\]

