The rate constant for each pathway is given by the Eyring equation  

\[
k=\frac{k_{\rm B}T}{h}\;e^{-\Delta G^{\ddagger}/RT}
\]

Since the prefactor \(\frac{k_{\rm B}T}{h}\) is identical for the α‑ and β‑paths, the ratio of the two rate constants is simply

\[
\frac{k_{\alpha}}{k_{\beta}}
   =\frac{e^{-\Delta G^{\ddagger}_{\alpha}/RT}}
          {e^{-\Delta G^{\ddagger}_{\beta}/RT}}
   =e^{-(\Delta G^{\ddagger}_{\alpha}-\Delta G^{\ddagger}_{\beta})/RT}
   =e^{-\Delta\Delta G^{\ddagger}/RT}.
\]

